--- a/SOURCE/BUILDING.TXT
+++ b/SOURCE/BUILDING.TXT
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+TANDI08 REPRODUCTION
+Use an isolated source directory and your licensed Microsoft C6/Windows inputs.
+Mount the toolchain as C: and SOURCE/src as D: in DOSBox-X. Run BUILD.BAT.
+The compile flags remain /G0 /Gw /AS. Check BUILD.OK, BUILD.LOG and TANDI.MAP.
+Run tools/AUDIT.PY with GNU objdump to audit the emitted NE code.
+Modern host tests need Python 3, GCC, Pillow and NumPy. They are not DOS inputs.
+Run tests/HOSTTEST.PY,tests/UIGUARD.PY,tests/DBTEST.PY,tests/CURTEST.PY,
+tests/QTEST06.PY,tests/AUDIT08.PY and tests/ROSTER.PY.
+Windows GCC builds run optimized mocks; sanitizer coverage is skipped there.
+On supported POSIX GCC builds the sound/UI mock sanitizer runs remain enabled.
+tests/ROSTER.PY accepts DAT path and output tag; it runs the actual C engine twice.
+Use build/TANDY.DAT CURRENT; build/AUDIT08.DAT AUDIT08; build/BASE128.DAT BASE128.
+tools/APPLY08.PY regenerates only the separate audited source/DAT after guards.
+Native tools/WINQA.PY requires these explicit environment variables:
+TANDI_PRIVATE=new private output parent; TANDI_WINDOWS=owned WINDOWS directory;
+TANDI_DOSBOX=emulator executable; TANDI_RESERVE=accepted RESERVE.COM;
+TANDI_TRIAL7=qualified TRIAL7 NEW driver directory; TANDI_LOCK=shared lock path.
+Every emulator collaborator must use the same lock, with a 60-second acquisition
+bound. Never remove another task's lock or kill another process.
+Run WINQA.PY 320x200x16 fresh-tag; repeat 640x200x2 and640x200x4.
+For bad-DAT: WINQA.PY 320x200x16 fresh-bad-tag bad.
+For saved-off startup: WINQA.PY 640x200x2 fresh-off-tag ok 0.
+The fourth argument selects initial sound preference 0 or 1.
+The fixture edits only private copies. Do not distribute the guest, OS, compiler,
+emulator or drivers through this standalone app packet. Captured Tandy app
+framebuffers and first-party code/data are the qualification evidence.
--- a/SOURCE/QA08.TXT
+++ b/SOURCE/QA08.TXT
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+TANDI08 / APP 0.3.5 LOCAL FOLLOW-UP QUALIFICATION
+
+Runtime fixes
+Thinking/worry is painted before synchronous engine work, with no 3/5-tick wait.
+The 220 ms post-compute guard and held-key/double-click protections remain.
+The Continue/Restart/Exit cap screen appears once per game after rejection at 25.
+After Continue, later rejections directly advance. All 256 remain reachable.
+F3 reads/writes WIN.INI [TANDINATOR] Sound. Unsupported NO SOUND, user SOUND OFF
+and a failed-write SOUND UNSAVED label are distinct. Missing setting defaults on.
+The app version is 0.3.5; standard roster revision is 0.3.2, not a character edition.
+Sound timing/ownership/cleanup module bytes are unchanged; no hardware lease bypass.
+
+Fresh verification
+Microsoft C6 /G0 /Gw /AS builds and links. WndProc remains exported.
+Emitted NE audit finds no unsupported or FPU instructions.
+45 extracted production-handler checks pass; 59 sound scenarios pass.
+Windows GCC sanitizer coverage was skipped; optimized mocks ran successfully.
+53 compiler/DAT tests pass. Standard curation/historical-delta tests pass.
+Three fresh Windows 3.0 real-mode runs pass: 320x200x16,640x200x2,640x200x4.
+They use 8086_prefetch,640 KB conventional,25,000 uncalibrated cycles, no FPU/XMS/EMS/UMB.
+Native tests verify all 130 question strings and 256 names, repeated input, overlays,
+cap continuation through all 256 candidates with one gate, preference read/write,
+and Escape/system-close/Exit-button cleanup followed by return to DOS.
+The 640x200x2 run starts with saved Sound=0. Mock settings-write failure/default
+fallback and unsupported-vs-off labels are covered separately.
+Actual corruptDAT gives repair/Exit only and returns to DOS.
+Native art checks pass in all modes: exact source indices, bounded moving eyes,
+byte-exact partial/border/focus redraws, 180 exact captured expression samples.
+Blink, thinking/worry, talking, happy/wink animation remains. The old decorative
+three-frame thinking wait is intentionally absent. Atlas artwork remains unchanged.
+Fresh DOS installer copies all four files and refuses to overwrite a sentinel.
+The installer code is identical to TANDI07; original installer coverage is inherited
+as well. No CF, installed defaults or user runtime directories were written.
+
+Separate experimental data proposal3
+Standard RUN/TANDY.DAT and source STARTER.JSON remain the pinned reviewed TANDI07.
+SOURCE/data/AUDIT08.JSON and SOURCE/build/AUDIT08.DAT are a separate 258-cell,
+21-character source-backed proposal. 255 UNKNOWN fills, Peppa red 0->4, Poseidon
+conquest 0->UNKNOWN and Messi Asia 0->UNKNOWN. All 64 cited source URLs are retained
+in PROPOSE.JSON; exact old/new cell guards and regeneration are in APPLY08.PY.
+No original 128 character source cells or question strings/IDs changed in the variant.
+ENGINE.C and DB.C remain byte-identical. Both DATs run twice through the same
+actual C engine/loader; all 256 targets remain reachable and each repeat is exact.
+Original cohort: 0 cap hits, 0 first misses; mean Q 9.3359375 ->9.3203125.
+Added cohort: 70->65 cap hits, 23->19 first misses, mean Q 19.4921875 ->18.875.
+Whole roster: 233->237 first guesses correct. These measure matrix self-consistency,
+not factual accuracy. Five misses improve, but a new Messi->Ronaldo miss remains.
+See COMPARE.JSN for every changed target and explicit regressions.
+The added cohort still averages 98.3359375 UNKNOWN answers out of 130 (75.64%).
+The full matrix still needs broader sourced coverage; this variant is not ready
+for standard/canonical promotion. No arbitrary yes/no or new geography question
+was introduced to force metrics. Broad association and artist semantics remain
+explicitly deferred in AUDIT08.JSN. Opposing-known pairs means opposing polarity;
+known-vs-UNKNOWN differences can still affect scores.
+
+Limits and handoff
+Native runtime qualification uses only the standard DAT; the separate data variant
+has host loader/engine and exact-delta qualification. No human play study, physical
+Tandy calibration or whole-roster factual certification is claimed.
+No engine threshold, extra questions, undo, loss reveal or canonical promotion.
+The newly supplied Claude harness remains outside this packet's implementation;
+its further policy comparison is a separate parent review.
+The first private fixture attempt missed trailing spaces in [boot] and timed out;
+the parser was fixed. An earlier successful UI run had FPU default on; explicit
+FPU-off runs replaced it. A help sentence clipped at 320; it was shortened and all
+final native runs were repeated. An active shared-lock open failure blocked one
+installer attempt; after the parent confirmed release, the same lease retry passed.
+Only final qualified app captures are packaged. Failed private attempts are retained
+locally in task-7/native-results, and are not presented as successful runs.
+Current main 0c1403088e347f2ebb8f4aef212c6953e525c921 was read-only confirmed by parent.
+Local clone base fc10cdea57f5cafb163b457648013829d08ab4a7 differs only in release
+workflow/FLASHDISK documentation, per parent connector comparison. TANDI paths
+match the verified packet. Network fetch was blocked; no denied action was bypassed.
+This is a local tested packet for review before publication. No push/PR/release/CF.
--- a/SOURCE/README.TXT
+++ b/SOURCE/README.TXT
@@ -1,9 +1,19 @@
-TANDINATOR 0.3.4 - USABILITY TRIAL
-Think of a character in ROSTER.TXT, using its named version.
-F1 Help. F2 Diagnostics (warns before showing candidate names). F3 Sound.
-Escape closes an overlay first; Escape elsewhere or EXIT closes the app.
-After a rejected guess at question 25, explicitly Continue guessing or Restart.
-No candidate is removed by a guess cap; the data and inference engine are unchanged.
-If TANDY.DAT cannot be read, exit, replace that file beside TANDI.EXE and restart.
-INSTALL.BAT copies the EXE, DAT, roster and this README without overwriting an
-existing installation. Start through your existing guarded WindowsXT launcher.
+TANDINATOR 0.3.5 - FOLLOW-UP UI TRIAL (TANDI08)
+Think of a character in ROSTER.TXT using its named character edition.
+App version is 0.3.5; the standard roster revision remains 0.3.2.
+F1 Help. F2 Diagnostics warns before candidate names. F3 Sound.
+F3 preference is stored in WIN.INI [TANDINATOR] Sound; answers are not saved.
+NO SOUND means unsupported hardware/mode/timer. SOUND OFF is your preference.
+SOUND UNSAVED means the preference could not be written; it still applies now.
+Escape closes an overlay first. Escape elsewhere or EXIT closes the app.
+Thinking is painted before prompt calculation, without a decorative timer wait.
+The 220 ms input guard, held-key and double-click protections are retained.
+After the first rejected guess at question 25, choose Continue, Restart or Exit.
+After Continue, later rejections directly advance; all candidates stay reachable.
+If TANDY.DAT cannot be read, exit, replace it beside TANDI.EXE and restart.
+INSTALL.BAT copies EXE,DAT,roster and README and refuses existing files.
+Use your existing guarded WindowsXT launcher; do not bypass its errors.
+This optional trial uses the reviewed standard 256-character/130-question DAT.
+The bounded AUDIT08 data proposal is separate in SOURCE/data and SOURCE/build.
+It is not promotion-ready. Read QA08.TXT and SOURCE/evidence/COMPARE.JSN.
+No engine threshold, extra questions, undo or canonical promotion is included.
